  "contract": "Secondary equality plans borrow matching ordered primary keys from the maintained index and resolve committed rows lazily. Staged inserts, predicate movements and deletes merge in key order; LIMIT and sink failure stop traversal. No matching-key vector or unrelated-row table scan is collected.",
  "canonical_values": "SQL index publication, deletion and lookup normalize descriptor-typed values consistently with physical rows. Int64 001 and boolean TRUE index as 1 and true. Staged indexed candidates also normalize before filtering. Typed catalog-backed library schemas are supported; native CREATE TABLE remains the existing text-column grammar.",
  "planning_sizes": "Derived committed row and encoded-byte counts update with row effects, including transaction commits, and rebuild from validated live KV on recovery. Tombstones are excluded. Fallback SELECT planning and row_count use these counts without scanning table keys. Explicit ANALYZE precedence is unchanged. Underflow/overflow rejects inconsistent metadata.",
  "compatibility": "No index key framing, durable SQL command/checkpoint/receipt version change or implicit data migration. Derived indexes are rebuilt on recovery. Existing request results/certificates and all prior regressions remain verified by the full gate.",
  "corruption": "A visited index reference to a missing row or mismatched indexed value rejects with CorruptionDetected, without a table-scan fallback. A stream encountering a source error cannot publish completion. Queries do not validate unrelated rows or matching candidates beyond LIMIT; cold recovery validates retained persisted state separately.",
  "baseline_failures": [
